-- title:
--   Horizontal unramifiedness of the full-level cover away from j=0,1728
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$ and a non-zero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero carrying a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$, together with the hypothesis that some ring homomorphism $L\to\mathbb{C}$ sends $\zeta$ to $\exp(2\pi i/q)$, and assume $L$ is algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L\subseteq L((T))$ obtained as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) of the function field of $X_H$ at level $q^2M'$ with $H=\ker\bigl((\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times\bigr)$, i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((T))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of that rational $q$-expansion field. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, acting on $K$ compatibly, and let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal. Let $j\in K$, non-zero, have Laurent image the coefficient embedding of the $q$-expansion $\mathrm{jq}$ of the modular invariant. Let $W_0$ be the valuation subring of $K$ consisting of those $f$ for which there are power series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ having non-zero reduction modulo the maximal ideal and $f\cdot y=x$ in $L((T))$. On the two-chart integral model $\mathcal{X}=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout glueing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the algebra of elements integral over $A[j]$ to the one for $A[j^{-1}]$, let $z$ be a point at which the germ $\varpi z$ of $\varpi$ (pulled back along the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$) lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and let $y$ be a point of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the finite chart algebra $B=$ `chartAlgFin A K j` mapping to $z$, with $y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ maximal. Let $\Omega$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ and $\varphi:B\to\Omega$ a ring homomorphism with kernel $y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, and assume $\varphi(j)\notin$ [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. some elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with invariant $\varphi(j)$ has a non-zero $q$-torsion point, and that every element of $B$ which is a non-unit of $W_0$ in $K$ lies in $y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$. Let $K_0\le K$ be the corresponding base change of the $\mathbb{Q}$-rational $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_0(M')$, with a non-zero $j_0\in K_0$ having the same Laurent image, with compatible $A$-algebra structure, and let $\iota:B_0=$ `chartAlgFin A K₀ j₀` $\to B$ be a ring homomorphism inducing the inclusion $K_0\hookrightarrow K$ on underlying elements. Assume finally $\varphi(j)\neq 0$ and $\varphi(j)\neq 1728$. Then, for the $B_0$-algebra structure on $B$ given by $\iota$, every prime ideal $\mathfrak{Q}\subseteq y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ of $B$ of height $1$ not containing the image of $\varpi$ satisfies `Algebra.IsUnramifiedAt B₀ 𝔔`.
--
--   This is the horizontal part of the ramification analysis of the full-level-$q$ cover of the $\Gamma_0(M')$ modular curve over a discrete valuation ring with residue characteristic $q$: at a height-one prime of the finite chart algebra lying in the closed point considered and not containing the uniformiser, the cover is unramified once the $j$-value there avoids $0$ and $1728$. It feeds the proof that the fibre of the integral model at an ordinary non-supersingular closed point is a regular local ring.
